{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "id": "test_gantry_repeatability",
  "display_name": "Test Gantry Repeatability",
  "category": "Robot Actions",
  "description": "Diagnostic for step-skipping. Using the last calibration, repeatedly tours X-min/Y-min -> X-mid/Y-max -> X-max/Y-min -> X-mid/Y-max at each test speed. X-min, X-max, and Y-min are real limit switches, so every arrival there is a genuine probe comparing the calibrated distance that should have been needed against how many steps it actually took to trip the switch. X-mid and Y-max have no limit switch (this machine only homes Y against Y-min) and are ordinary calibrated moves. Small, consistent deviation on every switch arrival means the motors are tracking commanded steps faithfully; growing or erratic deviation - especially at higher speeds - means steps are being skipped. Read-only: does not change the calibration.",
  "version": "0.2.0",
